PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L02U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":2,"cefr":"A1b","unit":2,"theme":"Food We Like","essential_question":"How do our food choices keep us healthy?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1","title":"I Don't Like Peas! Present Simple Negatives","objectives":["Students will be able to make present simple negatives with don't and doesn't.","Students will be able to use the base verb after don't and doesn't.","I can say \"I don't like peas\".","I can say \"He doesn't eat fish\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين النفي في المضارع البسيط باستخدام don't وdoesn't.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الفعل الأصلي بعد don't وdoesn't.","أستطيع أن أقول I don't like peas.","أستطيع أن أقول He doesn't eat fish."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/raɪs/","definition":"small white or brown grains we cook and eat","arabic":"أرز","example":"We eat rice with chicken.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"chicken","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɪkən/","definition":"meat from a bird that people keep on farms","arabic":"دجاج","example":"Mom grills chicken on Friday.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"fish","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɪʃ/","definition":"an animal that lives in water; its meat","arabic":"سمك","example":"Grilled fish is healthy.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"vegetables","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɛdʒtəbəlz/","definition":"plants we eat, like carrots and peas","arabic":"خضروات","example":"Fresh vegetables make us strong.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To make a present simple negative, use don't or doesn't + the base verb.\nUse don't (do not) with I, you, we, they. Use doesn't (does not) with he, she, it.\nThe -s goes on doesn't, so the main verb has no -s: He doesn't eat (NOT He doesn't eats).\nI / you / we / they + don't + base verb: We don't eat meat on Monday.\nhe / she / it + doesn't + base verb: She doesn't like coffee.\nNo -s after doesn't: it doesn't rain (NOT rains).","examples":["I don't like spicy food.","My dad doesn't drink coffee at night.","We don't eat in the living room.","The baby doesn't eat nuts.","Cats don't like water.","Lina doesn't take sugar in her tea.","You don't need a fork for a sandwich.","My grandparents don't cook on Friday."],"common_errors":["✗ He not like fish. → ✓ He doesn't like fish. (Use doesn't + verb.)","✗ She doesn't likes milk. → ✓ She doesn't like milk. (No -s after doesn't.)","✗ My brother don't eat eggs. → ✓ My brother doesn't eat eggs. (he/she/it → doesn't.)","✗ I no eat meat. → ✓ I don't eat meat. (Use don't, not no.)"],"arabic":"النفي في المضارع البسيط: don't مع I وyou وwe وthey، وdoesn't مع he وshe وit.\nبعد doesn't يأتي الفعل بدون s: He doesn't eat (وليس eats).\nلا نقول He not like أو I no eat، بل He doesn't like وI don't eat."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Don't Like Peas! Present Simple Negatives”. Let’s learn present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U2-LS1 | I Don't Like Peas! Present Simple Negatives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “What We Eat”: Hi, I'm Omar. My cousin Rakan doesn't like vegetables. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Hi, I'm Omar. My cousin Rakan doesn't like vegetables.","visual":"Image GV-L02-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To make a present simple negative, use don't or doesn't + the base verb. Use don't (do not) with I, you, we, they. Use doesn't (does not) with he, she, it.","on_screen":"I / you / we / they + don't + base verb: We don't eat meat on Monday. • he / she / it + doesn't + base verb: She doesn't like coffee. • No -s after doesn't: it doesn't rain (NOT rains).","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I don't like spicy food. My dad doesn't drink coffee at night. We don't eat in the living room.","on_screen":"I don't like spicy food. / My dad doesn't drink coffee at night. / We don't eat in the living room.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He not like fish.” That’s not right. We say: “He doesn't like fish.” Use doesn't + verb.","on_screen":"✗ He not like fish.   ✓ He doesn't like fish.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Rakan doesn't like vegetables.\" Is he happy when he sees carrots? … Think! … No, he isn't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I don't like peas\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I don't like peas\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","النفي في المضارع البسيط: don't مع I وyou وwe وthey، وdoesn't مع he وshe وit.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He not like fish. — الصحيح: He doesn't like fish.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I don't like peas."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"What We Eat","body":"Hi, I'm Omar. My cousin Rakan doesn't like vegetables. He doesn't eat carrots or peas. He loves rice and chicken.\nMy cousin Sara doesn't drink soda. She drinks water and fresh juice.\nI don't eat fast food every day. I like fruit, dates, and cheese.\nGrandpa doesn't put sugar in his tea.\nWe don't all like the same food, but we all love Grandma's kabsa!","word_count":65,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ like onions.","options":["not","don't","doesn't","no"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"My sister ___ eat meat.","options":["no","not","doesn't","don't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"He doesn't ___ cola.","options":["drink","to drink","drinks","drinking"],"answer":"drink","explanation":"No -s on the verb after don't/doesn't.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد doesn't."},{"q":"We ___ have lunch at home on school days.","options":["not","aren't","doesn't","don't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"My cat ___ eat vegetables.","options":["doesn't","don't","not","isn't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"They ___ cook fish at home.","options":["not","no","don't","doesn't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make the sentences negative.","items":[{"q":"Ali likes cheese.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"Ali doesn't like cheese.","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"We eat dinner at ten.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"We don't eat dinner at ten.","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"My mom drinks tea with milk.  (negative)","options":[],"answer":"My mom doesn't drink tea with milk.","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write don't or doesn't. Word bank: doesn't, don't","items":[{"q":"My cousins ______ like soup.","options":[],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"The shop ______ sell bread.","options":[],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"I ______ eat breakfast in the car.","options":[],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your food likes.","items":[{"q":"I don't like ___.","options":[],"answer":"I don't like mushrooms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My mom doesn't ___.","options":[],"answer":"My mom doesn't eat fast food.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My best friend doesn't like ___.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend doesn't like fish.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"We don't eat ___ for breakfast.","options":[],"answer":"We don't eat rice for breakfast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My little brother doesn't drink ___.","options":[],"answer":"My little brother doesn't drink coffee.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Food facts.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about food you and your family don't eat or drink.","options":[],"answer":"I don't eat spicy food. My dad doesn't drink soda. We don't eat late at night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 true negative facts about animals and food.","options":[],"answer":"Cows don't eat meat. A panda doesn't eat fish.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner what he doesn't like. Write 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Saad doesn't like eggs. He doesn't drink milk.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin & Speak","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Work in teams of four. Player 1 spins the wheel.","Make a correct sentence about the unit theme using the cue word and present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb).","The team checks the sentence with the grammar box. Correct = 1 point; an extra detail = 1 bonus point.","Pass the spinner clockwise. Play for 6 minutes; the team with most points wins."],"data":[{"label":"I"},{"label":"my dad"},{"label":"Sara"},{"label":"we"},{"label":"my cousins"},{"label":"the baby"},{"label":"you"},{"label":"Grandma"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I ___ eat candy every day.","options":["don't","doesn't","not","no"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"Grandpa ___ like loud music.","options":["not","don't","doesn't","isn't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"She doesn't ___ chocolate milk.","options":["like","liking","to like","likes"],"answer":"like","explanation":"No -s on the verb after don't/doesn't.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد doesn't."},{"q":"","options":["My brother don't eat breakfast.","My brother doesn't eat breakfast.","My brother doesn't eats breakfast.","My brother not eat breakfast."],"answer":"My brother doesn't eat breakfast.","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"We ___ go to restaurants on school nights.","options":["no","doesn't","don't","aren't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"","options":["Penguins don't eat bananas.","Penguins doesn't eat bananas.","Penguins don't eats bananas.","Penguins no eat bananas."],"answer":"Penguins don't eat bananas.","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"The café ___ open on Friday morning.","options":["not","don't","isn't","doesn't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"","options":["I not drink cold water in winter.","I doesn't drink cold water in winter.","I no drink cold water in winter.","I don't drink cold water in winter."],"answer":"I don't drink cold water in winter.","explanation":"Don't use no or not alone before the verb.","explanation_ar":"لا نستخدم no أو not وحدها قبل الفعل."},{"q":"My parents ___ like noisy places.","options":["not","don't","aren't","doesn't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"","options":["Reem not puts salt on her food.","Reem doesn't put salt on her food.","Reem doesn't puts salt on her food.","Reem don't put salt on her food."],"answer":"Reem doesn't put salt on her food.","explanation":"No -s on the verb after don't/doesn't.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد doesn't."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A family dinner table with kabsa in the middle; Omar's cousin Rakan pushing peas away, Grandpa drinking tea and Sara pouring water. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A family dinner table with kabsa in the middle; Omar's cousin Rakan pushing peas away, Grandpa drinking tea and Sara pouring water"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rice (small white or brown grains we cook and eat); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rice: small white or brown grains we cook and eat"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows chicken (meat from a bird that people keep on farms); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing chicken: meat from a bird that people keep on farms"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows fish (an animal that lives in water; its meat); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing fish: an animal that lives in water; its meat"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows vegetables (plants we eat, like carrots and peas); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing vegetables: plants we eat, like carrots and peas"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin & Speak”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin & Speak"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W01","script":"rice. rice. We eat rice with chicken.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W02","script":"chicken. chicken. Mom grills chicken on Friday.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W03","script":"fish. fish. Grilled fish is healthy.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-W04","script":"vegetables. vegetables. Fresh vegetables make us strong.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Hi, I'm Omar. My cousin Rakan doesn't like vegetables. He doesn't eat carrots or peas. He loves rice and chicken. My cousin Sara doesn't drink soda. She drinks water and fresh juice. I don't eat fast food every day. I like fruit, dates, and cheese. Grandpa doesn't put sugar in his tea. We don't all like the same food, but we all love Grandma's kabsa!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I Don't Like Peas! Present Simple Negatives”. Let’s learn present simple negative (don't / doesn't + verb) together. Listen to the start of “What We Eat”: Hi, I'm Omar. My cousin Rakan doesn't like vegetables. Look at the green words. To make a present simple negative, use don't or doesn't + the base verb. Use don't (do not) with I, you, we, they. Use doesn't (does not) with he, she, it. Here are some examples. I don't like spicy food. My dad doesn't drink coffee at night. We don't eat in the living room. Be careful! Some learners say: “He not like fish.” That’s not right. We say: “He doesn't like fish.” Use doesn't + verb. Quick check: \"Rakan doesn't like vegetables.\" Is he happy when he sees carrots? … Think! … No, he isn't. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I don't like peas\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2","title":"Do You Like Dates? Questions and Short Answers","objectives":["Students will be able to ask yes/no questions with Do and Does.","Students will be able to answer with short answers (Yes, I do. / No, she doesn't.).","I can ask \"Do you like dates?\" and \"Does she eat fish?\"","I can answer \"Yes, I do.\" and \"No, he doesn't.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة نعم/لا باستخدام Do وDoes.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الإجابة بإجابات قصيرة.","أستطيع أن أسأل Do you like dates? وDoes she eat fish?","أستطيع أن أجيب Yes, I do. وNo, he doesn't."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"fruit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frut/","definition":"food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes","arabic":"فاكهة","example":"I take fruit to school for a snack.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"dates","pos":"noun","ipa":"/deɪts/","definition":"sweet brown fruit from palm trees","arabic":"تمر","example":"We break our fast with dates.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"bread","pos":"noun","ipa":"/brɛd/","definition":"food made from flour and baked in an oven","arabic":"خبز","example":"The bread is warm and soft.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"cheese","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃiz/","definition":"a food made from milk","arabic":"جبن","example":"Lina likes white cheese with olives.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To ask a yes/no question in the present simple, start with Do or Does: Do you like dates? Does he eat fish?\nUse Do with I, you, we, they. Use Does with he, she, it. After Does, the verb has no -s: Does she like…? (NOT Does she likes…?)\nShort answers: Yes, I do. / No, I don't. Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't. We can also ask What questions: What do you eat for breakfast?","examples":["Do you like mangoes? – Yes, I do.","Does your dad cook? – Yes, he does.","Do they eat breakfast at school? – No, they don't.","Does the café sell sandwiches? – Yes, it does.","What do you drink in the morning? – I drink milk.","Does Noura like spicy food? – No, she doesn't.","Do we need more bread? – Yes, we do.","What does your cat eat? – It eats fish."],"common_errors":["✗ You like dates? → ✓ Do you like dates? (Start the question with Do.)","✗ Does he likes pizza? → ✓ Does he like pizza? (No -s after Does.)","✗ Is she eat fish? → ✓ Does she eat fish? (Use Does, not Is, with a main verb.)","✗ Do you like tea? – Yes, I like. → ✓ Yes, I do. (Short answer = do/does.)"],"arabic":"للسؤال في المضارع البسيط نبدأ بـ Do مع I وyou وwe وthey، وبـ Does مع he وshe وit.\nبعد Does يأتي الفعل بدون s: Does she like…? (وليس likes).\nلا نستخدم Is مع الفعل الأساسي: Does she eat…? (وليس Is she eat).\nالإجابة القصيرة: Yes, I do. / No, she doesn't."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Do You Like Dates? Questions and Short Answers”. Let’s learn present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U2-LS2 | Do You Like Dates? Questions and Short Answers","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: She likes rice. She doesn't like rice. Does she like rice? – Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't. • Do you eat fish? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • What do you have for lunch?","on_screen":"She likes rice. | She doesn't like rice. | Does she like rice? – Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't. • Do you eat fish? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • What do you have for lunch?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To ask a yes/no question in the present simple, start with Do or Does: Do you like dates? Does he eat fish? Use Do with I, you, we, they. Use Does with he, she, it. After Does, the verb has no -s: Does she like…? (NOT Does she likes…?)","on_screen":"present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Do you like mangoes? – Yes, I do. Does your dad cook? – Yes, he does. Do they eat breakfast at school? – No, they don't.","on_screen":"Do you like mangoes? – Yes, I do. / Does your dad cook? – Yes, he does. / Do they eat breakfast at school? – No, they don't.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You like dates?.” That’s not right. We say: “Do you like dates?.” Start the question with Do.","on_screen":"✗ You like dates?   ✓ Do you like dates?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which word starts a question about \"your mom\": Do or Does? … Think! … *Does* Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"Do you like dates?\" and \"Does she eat fish?\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"Do you like dates?\" and \"Does she eat fish?\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","للسؤال في المضارع البسيط نبدأ بـ Do مع I وyou وwe وthey، وبـ Does مع he وshe وit.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You like dates? — الصحيح: Do you like dates?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل Do you like dates? وDoes she eat fish?"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ you eat breakfast every day?","options":["Do","Is","Does","Are"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."},{"q":"___ your sister like olives?","options":["Is","Does","Are","Do"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"he / she / it → Does … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Does مع he وshe وit."},{"q":"Does he ___ milk at night?","options":["drinks","to drink","drinking","drink"],"answer":"drink","explanation":"No -s on the verb after Do/Does.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد Does."},{"q":"Do you like grapes? – Yes, I ___.","options":["am","does","do","like"],"answer":"do","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"Does Grandma bake cakes? – No, she ___.","options":["not","doesn't","don't","isn't"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"What ___ you have for lunch?","options":["are","does","do","is"],"answer":"do","explanation":"What do/does + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"What ثم do أو does ثم الفاعل والفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions.","items":[{"q":"You like honey.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Do you like honey?","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."},{"q":"Rakan eats salad.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Does Rakan eat salad?","explanation":"he / she / it → Does … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Does مع he وshe وit."},{"q":"They drink tea.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Do they drink tea?","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the short answers. Word bank: don't, does","items":[{"q":"Does your mom drink coffee? – Yes, she ______.","options":[],"answer":"does","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"Do your friends like pizza? – No, they ______.","options":[],"answer":"don't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"Does the restaurant open at noon? – Yes, it ______.","options":[],"answer":"does","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer the questions about you.","items":[{"q":"Do you like fish?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I do.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Does your dad cook?","options":[],"answer":"No, he doesn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you eat for breakfast?","options":[],"answer":"I eat eggs and bread.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do you drink juice every day?","options":[],"answer":"No, I don't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What does your family eat on Friday?","options":[],"answer":"We eat kabsa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Food survey.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 survey questions with Do you…?","options":[],"answer":"Do you like dates? Do you eat vegetables every day? Do you drink soda? Do you like spicy food?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask 3 classmates. Write their answers with he.","options":[],"answer":"Ali likes dates. Saad doesn't drink soda. Fahad eats vegetables every day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 What questions for your teacher.","options":[],"answer":"What do you eat for breakfast? What does your family cook on Friday?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Tic-Tac-Grammar","mechanic":"tic_tac_toe","rules":["Two teams: X and O. Team X chooses a square.","Using the cue, the team says a correct sentence with present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers (the form in brackets: +, – or ?).","If the class and teacher agree it is correct, the team marks the square.","Three squares in a row wins. Play a second round with the grid turned around."],"data":[{"cue":"he / like / carrots / –"},{"cue":"you / eat / fish / ?"},{"cue":"they / drink / coffee / –"},{"cue":"she / like / dates / ?"},{"cue":"I / eat / fast food / –"},{"cue":"your dad / cook / ?"},{"cue":"we / have / soup / –"},{"cue":"the baby / drink / milk / ?"},{"cue":"my sister / like / spicy food / –"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ they like chocolate?","options":["Are","Do","Is","Does"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."},{"q":"___ Ziyad eat rice every day?","options":["Is","Do","Does","Are"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"he / she / it → Does … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Does مع he وshe وit."},{"q":"Does she ___ fruit for a snack?","options":["has","having","have","to have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"No -s on the verb after Do/Does.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد Does."},{"q":"Do you drink milk? – No, I ___.","options":["am not","doesn't","not","don't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"","options":["Does your brother likes soup?","Do your brother like soup?","Is your brother like soup?","Does your brother like soup?"],"answer":"Does your brother like soup?","explanation":"he / she / it → Does … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Does مع he وshe وit."},{"q":"What ___ your cat eat?","options":["are","does","do","is"],"answer":"does","explanation":"What do/does + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"What ثم do أو does ثم الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"Does the baby sleep a lot? – Yes, he ___.","options":["sleeps","does","is","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"","options":["Do you and Majed eats lunch together?","Does you and Majed eat lunch together?","Do you and Majed eat lunch together?","Are you and Majed eat lunch together?"],"answer":"Do you and Majed eat lunch together?","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."},{"q":"","options":["What do your parents drink at breakfast?","What do your parents drinks at breakfast?","What your parents drink at breakfast?","What does your parents drink at breakfast?"],"answer":"What do your parents drink at breakfast?","explanation":"What do/does + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"What ثم do أو does ثم الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"Do you like spicy food? – ___","options":["Yes, I do.","Yes, I like.","Yes, I does.","Yes, I am."],"answer":"Yes, I do.","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two girls doing a food survey in the school canteen with clipboards, asking classmates questions in front of a menu board. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two girls doing a food survey in the school canteen with clipboards, asking classmates questions in front of a menu board"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Food We Like”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Food We Like”"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows fruit (food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing fruit: food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows dates (sweet brown fruit from palm trees); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing dates: sweet brown fruit from palm trees"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bread (food made from flour and baked in an oven); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bread: food made from flour and baked in an oven"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cheese (a food made from milk); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cheese: a food made from milk"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Tic-Tac-Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Tic-Tac-Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W01","script":"fruit. fruit. I take fruit to school for a snack.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W02","script":"dates. dates. We break our fast with dates.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W03","script":"bread. bread. The bread is warm and soft.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-W04","script":"cheese. cheese. Lina likes white cheese with olives.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Do You Like Dates? Questions and Short Answers”. Let’s learn present simple questions (Do/Does … ?) and short answers together. Remember these patterns: She likes rice. She doesn't like rice. Does she like rice? – Yes, she does. / No, she doesn't. • Do you eat fish? – Yes, I do. / No, I don't. • What do you have for lunch? To ask a yes/no question in the present simple, start with Do or Does: Do you like dates? Does he eat fish? Use Do with I, you, we, they. Use Does with he, she, it. After Does, the verb has no -s: Does she like…? (NOT Does she likes…?) Here are some examples. Do you like mangoes? – Yes, I do. Does your dad cook? – Yes, he does. Do they eat breakfast at school? – No, they don't. Be careful! Some learners say: “You like dates?.” That’s not right. We say: “Do you like dates?.” Start the question with Do. Quick check: Which word starts a question about \"your mom\": Do or Does? … Think! … *Does* Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"Do you like dates?\" and \"Does she eat fish?\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3","title":"Healthy and Delicious: Food Groups and Tastes","objectives":["Students will be able to sort food into groups (fruit, vegetables, grains, dairy, meat and fish, drinks).","Students will be able to describe food with taste words.","I can sort food into groups.","I can say if food is sweet, salty, sour or spicy."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تصنيف الأطعمة في مجموعات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف الطعام بكلمات المذاق.","أستطيع أن أصنّف الأطعمة في مجموعات.","أستطيع أن أقول إن الطعام حلو أو مالح أو حامض أو حار."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"juice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒus/","definition":"a drink made from fruit","arabic":"عصير","example":"Orange juice is full of vitamins.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"water","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɔtɚ/","definition":"the clear drink we need every day","arabic":"ماء","example":"Drink water when you are thirsty.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"healthy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhɛlθi/","definition":"good for your body","arabic":"صحي","example":"Soup is a healthy dinner.","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"delicious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dɪˈlɪʃəs/","definition":"tasting very good","arabic":"لذيذ","example":"This mango is delicious!","image_id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Food comes in groups: fruit (apples, dates), vegetables (carrots, cucumbers), grains (rice, bread), dairy (milk, cheese), meat and fish (chicken, fish) and drinks (water, juice).\nTaste words describe how food tastes: sweet (honey), salty (chips), sour (lemon), spicy (hot peppers). Delicious means it tastes very good.\nHealthy food is good for your body; unhealthy food is bad for your body if you eat too much of it. The prefix un- means \"not\".\nCollocations/phrases: fruit: dates, apples, grapes • vegetables: carrots, peas, cucumbers • grains: rice, bread, pasta | dairy: milk, cheese, yogurt • meat and fish: chicken, lamb, fish • drinks: water, juice, milk | sweet • salty • sour • spicy • delicious • healthy ↔ unhealthy","examples":["Dates are sweet and healthy.","A lemon tastes sour.","Chips are salty.","My uncle loves spicy food.","Cheese and yogurt are dairy foods.","Brown bread is a grain food.","Water is the best drink.","This chicken soup is delicious!"],"common_errors":["✗ Rice is a vegetable. → ✓ Rice is a grain. (Rice, bread and pasta are grains.)","✗ The lemon is sweet. → ✓ The lemon is sour. (Lemons taste sour.)","✗ Chips are very healthy. → ✓ Chips are unhealthy. (un- = not.)","✗ I want a breads. → ✓ I want some bread. (bread is not counted with a.)"],"arabic":"نصنّف الطعام في مجموعات: fruit (فاكهة) وvegetables (خضروات) وgrains (حبوب) وdairy (ألبان) وmeat (لحوم) وdrinks (مشروبات).\nكلمات المذاق: sweet (حلو) وsalty (مالح) وsour (حامض) وspicy (حار).\nالبادئة un تعني «غير»: unhealthy = غير صحي."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Healthy and Delicious: Food Groups and Tastes”. Let’s learn food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U2-LS3 | Healthy and Delicious: Food Groups and Tastes","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. juice: a drink made from fruit. water: the clear drink we need every day. healthy: good for your body.","on_screen":"juice | water | healthy","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Food comes in groups: fruit (apples, dates), vegetables (carrots, cucumbers), grains (rice, bread), dairy (milk, cheese), meat and fish (chicken, fish) and drinks (water, juice). Taste words describe how food tastes: sweet (honey), salty (chips), sour (lemon), spicy (hot peppers). Delicious means it tastes very good.","on_screen":"food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Dates are sweet and healthy. A lemon tastes sour. Chips are salty.","on_screen":"Dates are sweet and healthy. / A lemon tastes sour. / Chips are salty.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Rice is a vegetable.” That’s not right. We say: “Rice is a grain.” Rice, bread and pasta are grains.","on_screen":"✗ Rice is a vegetable.   ✓ Rice is a grain.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Is a lemon sweet or sour? … Think! … *Sour*. Great job! Now you can say: I can sort food into groups.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can sort food into groups.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نصنّف الطعام في مجموعات: fruit (فاكهة) وvegetables (خضروات) وgrains (حبوب) وdairy (ألبان) وmeat (لحوم) وdrinks (مشروبات).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Rice is a vegetable. — الصحيح: Rice is a grain.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصنّف الأطعمة في مجموعات."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Carrots and peas are ___.","options":["vegetables","fruit","drinks","dairy"],"answer":"vegetables","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Milk and cheese are ___ foods.","options":["meat","fruit","grain","dairy"],"answer":"dairy","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Honey tastes ___.","options":["sour","spicy","salty","sweet"],"answer":"sweet","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Hot peppers are ___.","options":["spicy","sour","soft","sweet"],"answer":"spicy","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Too much candy is ___.","options":["healthy","unhealthy","sour","salty"],"answer":"unhealthy","explanation":"un- means \"not\": unhealthy = not healthy.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"Sweet brown fruit from palm trees are ___.","options":["peas","grapes","dates","olives"],"answer":"dates","explanation":"Choose the food word that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the food to its group.","items":[{"q":"rice","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"grains","explanation":"rice → grains. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"yogurt","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"dairy","explanation":"yogurt → dairy. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"grapes","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"fruit","explanation":"grapes → fruit. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"cucumber","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"vegetables","explanation":"cucumber → vegetables. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"lamb","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"meat and fish","explanation":"lamb → meat and fish. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"orange juice","options":["dairy","grains","fruit","drinks","vegetables","meat and fish"],"answer":"drinks","explanation":"orange juice → drinks. Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your favorite foods.","items":[{"q":"My favorite fruit is ___. It is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite fruit is mango. It is sweet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A healthy breakfast is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A healthy breakfast is eggs, bread, and fruit.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A salty snack is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A salty snack is popcorn.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I think ___ is delicious.","options":[],"answer":"I think Grandma's soup is delicious.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An unhealthy food is ___.","options":[],"answer":"An unhealthy food is fried chips.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Plan a healthy lunchbox.","items":[{"q":"Draw a lunchbox with one food from 4 groups. Label them.","options":[],"answer":"brown bread (grain), cheese (dairy), apple (fruit), carrots (vegetables)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your lunchbox with taste words.","options":[],"answer":"My apple is sweet. The cheese is salty. The carrots are crunchy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with healthy and one with unhealthy.","options":[],"answer":"Water is healthy. Soda is unhealthy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"rice","match":"small white or brown grains we cook and eat","arabic":"أرز"},{"word":"chicken","match":"meat from a bird that people keep on farms","arabic":"دجاج"},{"word":"fish","match":"an animal that lives in water; its meat","arabic":"سمك"},{"word":"vegetables","match":"plants we eat, like carrots and peas","arabic":"خضروات"},{"word":"fruit","match":"food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes","arabic":"فاكهة"},{"word":"dates","match":"sweet brown fruit from palm trees","arabic":"تمر"},{"word":"bread","match":"food made from flour and baked in an oven","arabic":"خبز"},{"word":"cheese","match":"a food made from milk","arabic":"جبن"},{"word":"juice","match":"a drink made from fruit","arabic":"عصير"},{"word":"water","match":"the clear drink we need every day","arabic":"ماء"},{"word":"healthy","match":"good for your body","arabic":"صحي"},{"word":"delicious","match":"tasting very good","arabic":"لذيذ"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Chicken and fish are in the ___ group.","options":["grain","meat and fish","dairy","fruit"],"answer":"meat and fish","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Bread and pasta are ___.","options":["grains","dairy","drinks","vegetables"],"answer":"grains","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Lemons taste ___.","options":["salty","spicy","sweet","sour"],"answer":"sour","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Popcorn with lots of salt is ___.","options":["salty","sweet","sour","juicy"],"answer":"salty","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Fresh vegetables are ___.","options":["sour","unhealthy","healthy","spicy"],"answer":"healthy","explanation":"un- means \"not\": unhealthy = not healthy.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"un + healthy = ___","options":["unhealthy","inhealthy","not healthy un","healthyun"],"answer":"unhealthy","explanation":"un- means \"not\": unhealthy = not healthy.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"This cake tastes very good. It's ___.","options":["unhealthy","salty","sour","delicious"],"answer":"delicious","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"We drink ___ when we are thirsty.","options":["cheese","rice","bread","water"],"answer":"water","explanation":"Choose the food word that matches the clue.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام المناسبة."},{"q":"Which one is a dairy food?","options":["rice","chicken","yogurt","apple"],"answer":"yogurt","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Which one is a fruit?","options":["cheese","grapes","peas","bread"],"answer":"grapes","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A plate divided into colorful food groups – fruit, vegetables, rice and bread, cheese and milk, chicken and fish – with a glass of water beside it. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A plate divided into colorful food groups – fruit, vegetables, rice and bread, cheese and milk, chicken and fish – with a glass of water beside it"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows juice (a drink made from fruit); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing juice: a drink made from fruit"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows water (the clear drink we need every day); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing water: the clear drink we need every day"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows healthy (good for your body); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing healthy: good for your body"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows delicious (tasting very good); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing delicious: tasting very good"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W01","script":"juice. juice. Orange juice is full of vitamins.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W02","script":"water. water. Drink water when you are thirsty.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W03","script":"healthy. healthy. Soup is a healthy dinner.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-W04","script":"delicious. delicious. This mango is delicious!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Healthy and Delicious: Food Groups and Tastes”. Let’s learn food and drink categories; taste words (sweet, salty, sour, spicy) together. Meet some new words. juice: a drink made from fruit. water: the clear drink we need every day. healthy: good for your body. Food comes in groups: fruit (apples, dates), vegetables (carrots, cucumbers), grains (rice, bread), dairy (milk, cheese), meat and fish (chicken, fish) and drinks (water, juice). Taste words describe how food tastes: sweet (honey), salty (chips), sour (lemon), spicy (hot peppers). Delicious means it tastes very good. Here are some examples. Dates are sweet and healthy. A lemon tastes sour. Chips are salty. Be careful! Some learners say: “Rice is a vegetable.” That’s not right. We say: “Rice is a grain.” Rice, bread and pasta are grains. Quick check: Is a lemon sweet or sour? … Think! … *Sour*. Great job! Now you can say: I can sort food into groups.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4","title":"Monday to Sunday: Capital Letters for Days and Months","objectives":["Students will be able to write the days of the week and the months with capital letters.","Students will be able to capitalize holidays and Islamic months but not seasons.","I can write the days and months with capital letters.","I can write \"Eid al-Fitr\" and \"Ramadan\" correctly."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة أيام الأسبوع والشهور بحرف كبير.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير دون الفصول.","أستطيع أن أكتب الأيام والشهور بحرف كبير.","أستطيع أن أكتب Eid al-Fitr وRamadan بشكل صحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/raɪs/","definition":"small white or brown grains we cook and eat","arabic":"أرز","example":"We eat rice with chicken.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"chicken","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɪkən/","definition":"meat from a bird that people keep on farms","arabic":"دجاج","example":"Mom grills chicken on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fish","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɪʃ/","definition":"an animal that lives in water; its meat","arabic":"سمك","example":"Grilled fish is healthy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vegetables","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɛdʒtəbəlz/","definition":"plants we eat, like carrots and peas","arabic":"خضروات","example":"Fresh vegetables make us strong.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fruit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frut/","definition":"food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes","arabic":"فاكهة","example":"I take fruit to school for a snack.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dates","pos":"noun","ipa":"/deɪts/","definition":"sweet brown fruit from palm trees","arabic":"تمر","example":"We break our fast with dates.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"The days of the week always start with a capital letter: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.\nThe months start with a capital letter too: January, February, March… Islamic months and special days also need capitals: Ramadan, Shawwal, Eid al-Fitr, Saudi National Day.\nSeasons do not need a capital letter in the middle of a sentence: spring, summer, fall (US), winter.\nDays → capital: on Friday\nMonths → capital: in March\nHolidays and Islamic months → capitals: Eid al-Adha, Ramadan\nSeasons → small letters: in summer, in winter","examples":["We have a picnic on Friday.","School starts in September.","We fast in Ramadan.","Eid al-Fitr comes after Ramadan.","My birthday is in July.","It is very hot in summer.","Saudi National Day is on September 23.","We have art on Wednesday."],"common_errors":["✗ I go to my grandpa's house on friday. → ✓ I go to my grandpa's house on Friday. (Days need capital letters.)","✗ My birthday is in april. → ✓ My birthday is in April. (Months need capital letters.)","✗ In Winter, it rains in Taif. → ✓ In winter, it rains in Taif. (Seasons are small letters.)","✗ We eat dates in ramadan. → ✓ We eat dates in Ramadan. (Islamic months need capitals.)"],"arabic":"أيام الأسبوع والشهور تبدأ دائمًا بحرف كبير: Friday وJanuary.\nالأشهر الهجرية والأعياد بحرف كبير أيضًا: Ramadan وEid al-Fitr.\nالفصول الأربعة تُكتب بحرف صغير داخل الجملة: summer وwinter."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Monday to Sunday: Capital Letters for Days and Months”. Let’s learn capital letters for days of the week, months and special days together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U2-LS4 | Monday to Sunday: Capital Letters for Days and Months","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"The days of the week always start with a capital letter: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.","on_screen":"capital letters for days of the week, months and special days","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The days of the week always start with a capital letter: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday. The months start with a capital letter too: January, February, March… Islamic months and special days also need capitals: Ramadan, Shawwal, Eid al-Fitr, Saudi National Day.","on_screen":"Days → capital: on Friday • Months → capital: in March • Holidays and Islamic months → capitals: Eid al-Adha, Ramadan","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We have a picnic on Friday. School starts in September. We fast in Ramadan.","on_screen":"We have a picnic on Friday. / School starts in September. / We fast in Ramadan.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I go to my grandpa's house on friday.” That’s not right. We say: “I go to my grandpa's house on Friday.” Days need capital letters.","on_screen":"✗ I go to my grandpa's house on friday.   ✓ I go to my grandpa's house on Friday.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Does \"summer\" need a capital letter in the middle of a sentence? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can write the days and months with capital letters.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write the days and months with capital letters.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters for days of the week, months and special days.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أيام الأسبوع والشهور تبدأ دائمًا بحرف كبير: Friday وJanuary.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I go to my grandpa's house on friday. — الصحيح: I go to my grandpa's house on Friday.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب الأيام والشهور بحرف كبير."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Busy Month (editing passage)","body":"In november, I have a lot to do. On sunday, I go to the library. On wednesday, I have a swimming lesson. In Fall, the weather in Taif is cool. My cousin's wedding is on friday.","word_count":36,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["We Go shopping on Thursday.","we go shopping on thursday.","We go shopping on thursday.","We go shopping on Thursday."],"answer":"We go shopping on Thursday.","explanation":"Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["my sister's birthday is in May","My sister's birthday is in May.","My Sister's birthday is in may.","My sister's birthday is in may."],"answer":"My sister's birthday is in May.","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We visit Makkah in Ramadan.","We visit Makkah in ramadan.","we visit makkah in Ramadan.","We visit makkah in ramadan."],"answer":"We visit Makkah in Ramadan.","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["It snows in some countries in Winter.","It Snows in some countries in winter.","it snows in some countries in Winter.","It snows in some countries in winter."],"answer":"It snows in some countries in winter.","explanation":"Seasons are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الفصول بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["Eid al-Adha is a happy day.","eid al-Adha is a happy day.","eid al-adha is a happy day.","Eid Al-adha is a happy day."],"answer":"Eid al-Adha is a happy day.","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The test is on tuesday, March 4.","The test is on tuesday, march 4.","The test is on Tuesday, March 4.","The test is on Tuesday, march 4."],"answer":"The test is on Tuesday, March 4.","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the capital letter mistake.","items":[{"q":"We play football on monday.","options":[],"answer":"We play football on Monday.","explanation":"monday → Monday. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: monday → Monday. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Our school trip is in october.","options":[],"answer":"Our school trip is in October.","explanation":"october → October. Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: october → October. الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"I love the flowers in Spring.","options":[],"answer":"I love the flowers in spring.","explanation":"Spring → spring. Seasons are small letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Spring → spring. الفصول بحرف صغير."},{"q":"My family visits Grandma on saturday.","options":[],"answer":"My family visits Grandma on Saturday.","explanation":"saturday → Saturday. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: saturday → Saturday. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"shawwal comes after Ramadan.","options":[],"answer":"Shawwal comes after Ramadan.","explanation":"shawwal → Shawwal. Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: shawwal → Shawwal. الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The new mall opens in december.","options":[],"answer":"The new mall opens in December.","explanation":"december → December. Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: december → December. الشهور بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit Lina's calendar note.","items":[{"q":"In november, I have a lot to do.","options":[],"answer":"In November, I have a lot to do.","explanation":"november → November. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: november → November. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"On sunday, I go to the library.","options":[],"answer":"On Sunday, I go to the library.","explanation":"sunday → Sunday. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: sunday → Sunday. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"On wednesday, I have a swimming lesson.","options":[],"answer":"On Wednesday, I have a swimming lesson.","explanation":"wednesday → Wednesday. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: wednesday → Wednesday. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"In Fall, the weather in Taif is cool.","options":[],"answer":"In fall, the weather in Taif is cool.","explanation":"Fall → fall. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Fall → fall. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My cousin's wedding is on friday.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin's wedding is on Friday.","explanation":"friday → Friday. Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: friday → Friday. أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your calendar.","items":[{"q":"Write your favorite day of the week and why.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite day is Friday because I visit my grandparents.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for days of the week, months and special days correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the month of your birthday and one special day in that month.","options":[],"answer":"My birthday is in June. My cousin's birthday is in June too.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for days of the week, months and special days correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about Ramadan or Eid.","options":[],"answer":"We fast in Ramadan. We wear new clothes on Eid al-Fitr.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for days of the week, months and special days correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Builder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The teacher reads a word and a short clue.","Teams build the word with letter tiles in 30 seconds.","The team holds up the word; correct spelling = 1 point, with correct capital letter or punctuation where needed = 1 bonus point.","Continue until all words are used."],"data":[{"word":"Monday","clue":""},{"word":"Wednesday","clue":""},{"word":"Thursday","clue":""},{"word":"Saturday","clue":""},{"word":"February","clue":""},{"word":"Ramadan","clue":""},{"word":"rice","clue":"small white or brown grains we cook and eat"},{"word":"chicken","clue":"meat from a bird that people keep on farms"},{"word":"fish","clue":"an animal that lives in water; its meat"},{"word":"vegetables","clue":"plants we eat, like carrots and peas"},{"word":"fruit","clue":"food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes"},{"word":"dates","clue":"sweet brown fruit from palm trees"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["My uncle arrives on Wednesday.","my uncle arrives on Wednesday","My uncle arrives on wednesday.","My Uncle arrives on wednesday."],"answer":"My uncle arrives on Wednesday.","explanation":"Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which word needs a capital letter?","options":["winter","january","fall","spring"],"answer":"january","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We eat dates in Ramadan.","We eat Dates in ramadan.","We eat dates in ramadan.","we eat dates in Ramadan."],"answer":"We eat dates in Ramadan.","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The weather is hot in summer.","the weather is hot in Summer.","The weather is hot in Summer.","The Weather is hot in summer."],"answer":"The weather is hot in summer.","explanation":"Seasons are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الفصول بحرف صغير."},{"q":"Which word does NOT need a capital letter?","options":["Eid","Monday","August","winter"],"answer":"winter","explanation":"Seasons are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الفصول بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["Saudi national day is in September.","saudi national day is in september.","Saudi National Day is in September.","Saudi National Day is in september."],"answer":"Saudi National Day is in September.","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"we have a test on tuesday.\"","options":["3","0","2","1"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["school starts in August or September.","School starts in august or september.","School starts in August or september.","School starts in August or September."],"answer":"School starts in August or September.","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["On Saturday, We go to the beach.","On Saturday, we go to the beach.","On saturday, we go to the beach.","on Saturday, we go to the beach."],"answer":"On Saturday, we go to the beach.","explanation":"Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["eid al-fitr","Eid al-Fitr","Eid Al-fitr","eid Al-Fitr"],"answer":"Eid al-Fitr","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Food We Like” that shows capital letters for days of the week, months and special days in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Food We Like” that shows capital letters for days of the week, months and special days in action"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Builder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Builder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Monday to Sunday: Capital Letters for Days and Months”. Let’s learn capital letters for days of the week, months and special days together. The days of the week always start with a capital letter: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday. The days of the week always start with a capital letter: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday. The months start with a capital letter too: January, February, March… Islamic months and special days also need capitals: Ramadan, Shawwal, Eid al-Fitr, Saudi National Day. Here are some examples. We have a picnic on Friday. School starts in September. We fast in Ramadan. Be careful! Some learners say: “I go to my grandpa's house on friday.” That’s not right. We say: “I go to my grandpa's house on Friday.” Days need capital letters. Quick check: Does \"summer\" need a capital letter in the middle of a sentence? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can write the days and months with capital letters.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5","title":"My Food Diary: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to ask and answer questions about food habits.","Students will be able to write a food diary using the present simple and days of the week.","I can ask a friend about the food he eats.","I can write my food diary."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة عن العادات الغذائية والإجابة عنها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة مذكرات طعام بالمضارع البسيط وأيام الأسبوع.","أستطيع أن أسأل صديقي عن الطعام الذي يأكله.","أستطيع أن أكتب مذكرات طعامي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"rice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/raɪs/","definition":"small white or brown grains we cook and eat","arabic":"أرز","example":"We eat rice with chicken.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"chicken","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɪkən/","definition":"meat from a bird that people keep on farms","arabic":"دجاج","example":"Mom grills chicken on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fish","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɪʃ/","definition":"an animal that lives in water; its meat","arabic":"سمك","example":"Grilled fish is healthy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"vegetables","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvɛdʒtəbəlz/","definition":"plants we eat, like carrots and peas","arabic":"خضروات","example":"Fresh vegetables make us strong.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fruit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/frut/","definition":"food from trees and plants, like apples and grapes","arabic":"فاكهة","example":"I take fruit to school for a snack.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"dates","pos":"noun","ipa":"/deɪts/","definition":"sweet brown fruit from palm trees","arabic":"تمر","example":"We break our fast with dates.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bread","pos":"noun","ipa":"/brɛd/","definition":"food made from flour and baked in an oven","arabic":"خبز","example":"The bread is warm and soft.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cheese","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tʃiz/","definition":"a food made from milk","arabic":"جبن","example":"Lina likes white cheese with olives.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"juice","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒus/","definition":"a drink made from fruit","arabic":"عصير","example":"Orange juice is full of vitamins.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"water","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɔtɚ/","definition":"the clear drink we need every day","arabic":"ماء","example":"Drink water when you are thirsty.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"healthy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhɛlθi/","definition":"good for your body","arabic":"صحي","example":"Soup is a healthy dinner.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"delicious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/dɪˈlɪʃəs/","definition":"tasting very good","arabic":"لذيذ","example":"This mango is delicious!","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the present simple (positive, negative and questions), food words, taste words and capital letters for days and months.\nA food diary lists what you eat each day. It uses the present simple because it shows habits.\n✔ I eat / he eats – I don't eat / he doesn't eat\n✔ Do you…? Does he…? + short answers\n✔ food groups and taste words\n✔ capital letters for days and months","examples":["On Thursday, we eat pizza.","My dad doesn't eat sugar.","Do you like yogurt? – Yes, I do.","Grapes are sweet and juicy.","My grandma makes bread on Friday.","We don't drink soda at home.","Does your sister eat breakfast? – No, she doesn't.","In Ramadan, we eat dates and soup at sunset."],"common_errors":["✗ On monday I eat fish. → ✓ On Monday, I eat fish. (Capital for the day; a comma after a time phrase at the start helps the reader.)","✗ My sister don't eats meat. → ✓ My sister doesn't eat meat. (doesn't + base verb.)","✗ You eat fish on Friday? → ✓ Do you eat fish on Friday? (Start with Do.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع البسيط بالإثبات والنفي والسؤال، وكلمات الطعام، والحروف الكبيرة للأيام.\nمذكرات الطعام تستخدم المضارع البسيط لأنها عادات.\nلا تنسَ: doesn't + الفعل الأصلي، وDoes في بداية السؤال."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Food Diary: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L02-U2-LS5 | My Food Diary: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Healthy or unhealthy? In pairs, ask \"Do you eat… every day? Does your family…?\" Then decide together if your partner's week is healthy and give one tip.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: the present simple (positive, negative and questions), food words, taste words and capital letters for days and months. A food diary lists what you eat each day. It uses the present simple because it shows habits.","on_screen":"✔ I eat / he eats – I don't eat / he doesn't eat • ✔ Do you…? Does he…? + short answers • ✔ food groups and taste words","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. On Thursday, we eat pizza. My dad doesn't eat sugar. Do you like yogurt? – Yes, I do.","on_screen":"On Thursday, we eat pizza. / My dad doesn't eat sugar. / Do you like yogurt? – Yes, I do.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “On monday I eat fish.” That’s not right. We say: “On Monday, I eat fish.” Capital for the day; a comma after a time phrase at the start helps the reader.","on_screen":"✗ On monday I eat fish.   ✓ On Monday, I eat fish.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “My sister don't eats meat.”? … Think! … It should be “My sister doesn't eat meat.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask a friend about the food he eats.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask a friend about the food he eats.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع البسيط بالإثبات والنفي والسؤال، وكلمات الطعام، والحروف الكبيرة للأيام.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: On monday I eat fish. — الصحيح: On Monday, I eat fish.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل صديقي عن الطعام الذي يأكله."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Food Diary – Sara","body":"On Monday, I have cheese, bread, and tea for breakfast.\nI don't drink soda. I drink water and juice.\nOn Tuesday, my mom cooks fish. It is delicious!\nOn Wednesday, we eat chicken and rice. My brother doesn't like the vegetables, but I do.\nDo you eat healthy food?","word_count":49,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Sara's diary. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Sara has cheese and bread for breakfast on Monday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara drinks soda every day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Her mom cooks fish on Tuesday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They eat chicken and rice on Thursday.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara's brother likes the vegetables.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara likes the vegetables.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Food Diary – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Sara's mom ___ fish on Tuesday.","options":["cook","cooking","is cook","cooks"],"answer":"cooks","explanation":"he/she/it + verb-s; I/you/we/they + base verb.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Sara's brother ___ like vegetables.","options":["don't","doesn't","isn't","not"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"don't/doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ don't أو doesn't."},{"q":"___ Sara drink water? – Yes, she does.","options":["Is","Do","Does","Are"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"Do/Does + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Do أو Does."},{"q":"Lemons are ___.","options":["spicy","salty","sour","sweet"],"answer":"sour","explanation":"Choose the right food or taste word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام أو المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["We have fish on Tuesday.","we have fish on Tuesday","We have fish on tuesday.","We Have fish on tuesday."],"answer":"We have fish on Tuesday.","explanation":"Days, months and holidays start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأيام والشهور والأعياد بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Rice and bread are ___.","options":["dairy","fruit","drinks","grains"],"answer":"grains","explanation":"Choose the right food or taste word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام أو المذاق المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Interview a partner about his food week.","items":[{"q":"Ask: \"What do you eat for breakfast?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"He eats eggs and bread.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Do you drink soda?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"No, he doesn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"What does your family eat on Friday?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"His family eats kabsa on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Do you eat vegetables every day?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he does.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is his week healthy? Give him one tip with \"Eat…\" or \"Don't…\".","options":[],"answer":"Yes, it is. Don't eat too many chips.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your food diary.","items":[{"q":"Plan: choose 3 days and write what you eat and drink.","options":[],"answer":"Sunday – eggs, juice; Monday – chicken, rice; Tuesday – fish, salad","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 5–6 sentences. Use one negative and one question.","options":[],"answer":"On Sunday, I eat eggs for breakfast. On Monday, we have chicken and rice. I don't drink soda. On Tuesday, my mom cooks fish. It is delicious! Do you like fish?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: verbs with -s? don't/doesn't? capital letters for days? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"on sunday\" to \"on Sunday\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Quiz Show Challenge","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams take turns choosing a category and a cue word.","Grammar: make a sentence with present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review). Words: give the meaning. Spelling: spell it. Write It!: write a sentence with correct punctuation.","Correct answers score 10 points; teams may steal a question another team misses.","The highest score after 8 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"rice","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"chicken","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"fish","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"vegetables","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"fruit","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"dates","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bread","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cheese","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"juice","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"water","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"healthy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"delicious","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My uncle ___ in a restaurant. (work)","options":["works","work","is work","working"],"answer":"works","explanation":"he/she/it + verb-s; I/you/we/they + base verb.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"We ___ eat sweets before dinner.","options":["no","doesn't","aren't","don't"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"don't/doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ don't أو doesn't."},{"q":"___ your brother like cheese?","options":["Does","Do","Is","Are"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"Do/Does + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Do أو Does."},{"q":"","options":["Does Hamad drinks milk? – No, he doesn't.","Is Hamad drink milk? – No, he isn't.","Does Hamad drink milk? – No, he doesn't.","Do Hamad drink milk? – No, he don't."],"answer":"Does Hamad drink milk? – No, he doesn't.","explanation":"Do/Does + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Do أو Does."},{"q":"Chips are ___.","options":["sour","salty","sweet","juicy"],"answer":"salty","explanation":"Choose the right food or taste word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام أو المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["We eat lunch late on Friday.","We eat lunch late on friday.","We eats lunch late on Friday.","we eat lunch late on friday."],"answer":"We eat lunch late on Friday.","explanation":"Days, months and holidays start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأيام والشهور والأعياد بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which one is unhealthy if you eat a lot?","options":["apples","carrots","candy","water"],"answer":"candy","explanation":"Choose the right food or taste word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة الطعام أو المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["My cousins don't eats spicy food.","My cousins not eat spicy food.","My cousins doesn't eat spicy food.","My cousins don't eat spicy food."],"answer":"My cousins don't eat spicy food.","explanation":"don't/doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"النفي بـ don't أو doesn't."},{"q":"What ___ she eat for a snack? – An apple.","options":["are","does","do","is"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Do/Does + subject + base verb?","explanation_ar":"السؤال بـ Do أو Does."},{"q":"Choose the best diary sentence:","options":["On Sunday, I am have yogurt and dates.","On sunday, I has yogurt and dates.","on Sunday I have yogurt, dates","On Sunday, I have yogurt and dates."],"answer":"On Sunday, I have yogurt and dates.","explanation":"Days, months and holidays start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأيام والشهور والأعياد بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Sara writing in a colorful food diary at the kitchen table with a plate of fruit, a glass of milk and a calendar on the wall. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara writing in a colorful food diary at the kitchen table with a plate of fruit, a glass of milk and a calendar on the wall"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Food We Like”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Food We Like”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L02-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Quiz Show Challenge”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Quiz Show Challenge"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS5-T1","script":"On Monday, I have cheese, bread, and tea for breakfast. I don't drink soda. I drink water and juice. On Tuesday, my mom cooks fish. It is delicious! On Wednesday, we eat chicken and rice. My brother doesn't like the vegetables, but I do. Do you eat healthy food?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L02-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Food Diary: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple (positive, negative, questions), food words and capital letters for days (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Healthy or unhealthy? In pairs, ask \"Do you eat… every day? Does your family…?\" Then decide together if your partner's week is healthy and give one tip. Today you use all of Unit 2: the present simple (positive, negative and questions), food words, taste words and capital letters for days and months. A food diary lists what you eat each day. It uses the present simple because it shows habits. Here are some examples. On Thursday, we eat pizza. My dad doesn't eat sugar. Do you like yogurt? – Yes, I do. Be careful! Some learners say: “On monday I eat fish.” That’s not right. We say: “On Monday, I eat fish.” Capital for the day; a comma after a time phrase at the start helps the reader. Quick check: what is wrong with “My sister don't eats meat.”? … Think! … It should be “My sister doesn't eat meat.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask a friend about the food he eats.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My grandparents ___ like noisy restaurants.","options":["no","doesn't","don't","not"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"The baby ___ eat nuts.","options":["don't","doesn't","isn't","not"],"answer":"doesn't","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"He doesn't ___ coffee.","options":["to drink","drinking","drink","drinks"],"answer":"drink","explanation":"No -s on the verb after don't/doesn't.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد doesn't."},{"q":"","options":["I don't eat fish on Monday.","I don't eats fish on Monday.","I not eat fish on Monday.","I doesn't eat fish on Monday."],"answer":"I don't eat fish on Monday.","explanation":"I / you / we / they → don't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع I وyou وwe وthey نستخدم don't."},{"q":"","options":["Lina don't like sour fruit.","Lina not like sour fruit.","Lina doesn't likes sour fruit.","Lina doesn't like sour fruit."],"answer":"Lina doesn't like sour fruit.","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"___ your friends eat lunch at school?","options":["Are","Do","Does","Is"],"answer":"Do","explanation":"I / you / we / they → Do … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Do مع I وyou وwe وthey."},{"q":"___ your dad cook on Friday?","options":["Does","Do","Is","Are"],"answer":"Does","explanation":"he / she / it → Does … ?","explanation_ar":"نستخدم Does مع he وshe وit."},{"q":"Does she ___ fruit every day?","options":["eats","to eat","eat","eating"],"answer":"eat","explanation":"No -s on the verb after don't/doesn't.","explanation_ar":"لا نضيف s للفعل بعد doesn't."},{"q":"Do you like olives? – No, I ___.","options":["don't","doesn't","not","am not"],"answer":"don't","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."},{"q":"What ___ your brother drink at night?","options":["is","does","are","do"],"answer":"does","explanation":"What do/does + subject + verb?","explanation_ar":"What ثم do أو does ثم الفاعل والفعل."},{"q":"Carrots are ___.","options":["fruit","grains","dairy","vegetables"],"answer":"vegetables","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Milk, cheese and yogurt are ___ foods.","options":["meat","grain","fruit","dairy"],"answer":"dairy","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"Honey is ___.","options":["salty","sour","sweet","spicy"],"answer":"sweet","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Too much soda is ___.","options":["unhealthy","healthy","salty","sour"],"answer":"unhealthy","explanation":"un- means \"not\": unhealthy = not healthy.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"This pizza is so good! It's ___.","options":["salty","sour","delicious","unhealthy"],"answer":"delicious","explanation":"Choose the taste word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المذاق المناسبة."},{"q":"Which one is a grain food?","options":["fish","bread","yogurt","grapes"],"answer":"bread","explanation":"Think about the food group.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مجموعة الطعام."},{"q":"","options":["We Visit our cousins on Thursday.","We visit our cousins on Thursday.","we visit our cousins on thursday.","We visit our cousins on thursday."],"answer":"We visit our cousins on Thursday.","explanation":"Days of the week start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أيام الأسبوع بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["My brother was born in October.","My brother was born in october.","my brother was born in October","My Brother was born in october."],"answer":"My brother was born in October.","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["it rains a lot in Winter.","It Rains a lot in winter.","It rains a lot in winter.","It rains a lot in Winter."],"answer":"It rains a lot in winter.","explanation":"Seasons are small letters.","explanation_ar":"الفصول بحرف صغير."},{"q":"Which one needs capital letters?","options":["fall","summer","spring","eid al-fitr"],"answer":"eid al-fitr","explanation":"Holidays and Islamic months need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأعياد والأشهر الهجرية بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"my party is on saturday in july.\"","options":["1","2","4","3"],"answer":"3","explanation":"Months start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الشهور بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a food diary:","options":["On Friday, my dad makes pancakes.","On Friday, my dad is make pancakes.","On friday, my dad make pancakes.","on Friday my dad makes pancake."],"answer":"On Friday, my dad makes pancakes.","explanation":"he/she/it + verb-s; I/you/we/they + base verb.","explanation_ar":"المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"she don't like eggs.\"","options":["She doesn't likes eggs.","she doesn't like eggs.","She don't like eggs.","She doesn't like eggs."],"answer":"She doesn't like eggs.","explanation":"he / she / it → doesn't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"مع he وshe وit نستخدم doesn't."},{"q":"Do your parents drink tea? – ___","options":["Yes, they drink.","Yes, they do.","Yes, they does.","Yes, they are."],"answer":"Yes, they do.","explanation":"Short answers: Yes, I do / No, he doesn't.","explanation_ar":"الإجابة القصيرة بـ do وdoes."}],"theme_ar":"الطعام الذي نحبه","essential_question_ar":"كيف تساعدنا اختياراتنا للطعام على البقاء أصحّاء؟","can_do":"I can say what people like and don't like to eat, and ask and answer questions about food.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقول ما يحبه الناس وما لا يحبونه من الطعام، وأسأل وأجيب عن الطعام."});
